 these robberies were all  being committed by the same gang after  all the criminals didn't really make an  effort to hide their identities and  there was one person that stood out to  all the witnesses a short guy with  blonde hair and deep blue eyes and the  cherubic look of an innocent youngster  and anonymous tip from the Chicago  underworld even got the police a name  George Nelson doctor called Babyface and  big George behind his back rounding up  the suspects wasn't exactly the work of  Kojak as we said the crew didn't come  cover their tracks very well by February  1931 Nelson and his two main accomplices  were in custody all taken in without a  fight they had been identified by a few  dozen Witnesses so the case against them  was as solid as granite and the police  chief was cheerfully touting the arrest  of the stick up Trio as among the most  important in the police history of  Chicago one of the subordinates even  included the Babyface name in the  official press release for the media  thus ensuring that Nelson would forever  be immortalized by the moniker that he  hated most the trial went about as well  as you'd expect one of the Three Robbers  testified against the other two in  exchange for probation the other pled  guilty for a reduced sentence only  Nelson refused to deal he insisted that  he was innocent but the jury wasn't  taken in by his boyish charm they took  less than two hours to find him guilty  Nelson was then sentenced to one year to  life in the state prison a Joliet  foreign  spent less than one year in prison in  February 1932 it was due to stand trial  for a solo robbery but for some reason  the authorities concluded that a single  Burly prison guard would be enough to  keep an eye on the diminutive delinquent  the duo was riding the train back to  Joliet when Nelson managed to get his  hands on a 45 automatic most likely  hidden by an accomplice Babyface took  the guard and a taxi driver hostage and  drove to the middle of nowhere that's  when he told them to get out and he rode  off alone into the sunset with the law  in his tail Nelson fled Illinois and  made his way to Reno Nevada he didn't  spend a lot of time there but enough for  him to Pal around with some other  prominent Outlaws of that era such as  Alvin karpis who ran the Barker gang and  Eddie benster Confederate of Machine Gun  Kelly they pulled off several heists  together this time traveling from state  to state instead of staying in the same  place and making it as far north as  Minnesota however it was in Sausalito  California that Nelson made the  acquaintance of John Paul chase the man  who would become his new partner in  crime until The Bitter End after  bullying a few scores with more various  bank robbers like carpers and bents  Nelson gained the confidence to start  his own crew Chase was his right-hand  man and other members included Eddie  Green Tommy Carroll and Homer Van Meter  together they executed a string of  robberies all across the country most  notorious was other one in Brainerd  Minnesota feeling cocky following a  textbook bank heist the gang wanted to  leave guns blazing literally Nelson and  Van Meter stuck their tommy guns out the  windows of their getaway car as they  sped out of town and sprayed both sides  of the street bullets they smashed  dozens of stores and car windows but  through some miracle they didn't hit a  single person not that fatalities would  have bothered them too much the gang  soon claimed their first known victim in  a gunfight with San Antonio police were  detective Henry perro was shot and  killed as to the trigger man Witnesses  claimed Tommy Carroll was the killer but  he was never positively id'd that is  pretty much how Nelson and his gang  spent 1933. although George's wife never  participated in any of the robberies she  accepted that this was who he was and  often followed him around with the kids  so the family could spend time together  when Evan Nelson was laying low it was  during this time that Nelson met with  another Leading Light of the underworld  someone the Van Meter did dine with back  in Indiana John Dillinger the two gangs  met up at a safe house in Chicago their  little gathering was cordial enough they  swapped Adventures they exchanged useful  contacts and they drank all except  Nelson he never touched alcohol after  what he did to his father and that  always about it  at least for the time being  now that if you've seen our biographics  video on John Dillinger you would know  that the Dillinger gang had two distinct  incarnations in January 1934 the first  crew was captured in Tucson Arizona and  all the original members found  themselves in prison except for one guy  named red Hamilton like Dillinger  Hamilton was on good terms with Van  Meter and with nowhere else to turn to  he joined up with Nelson's gang after  all as far as he knew none of his former  compatriots would see life outside the  Prison Walls ever again with some of  them even scoring a date with the  electric chair but John Dillinger  escaped prison in early March perhaps  even with Hamilton's help and was  itching to stick up a few Banks the old  gang was gone but Hamilton had already  hooked up with a new crew the only  question was could dylinder and Nelson  get along here are two guys who both  wanted to be the leader are one of them  with a serious overcompensation problem  they had what you would call A Clash of  personalities and Nelson was none to  please whenever other gang members would  turn to Dillinger instead of him since  he liked to think that he was the one in  charge he probably blew a gasket when he  saw the newspapers referring to the  group as the Dillinger gang and he  reacted rather predictably with violence  it was at this time that baby first  Nelson fully embraced his dark side and  turned into the most ruthless man in the  country even before pulling off their  first Heist Nelson killed a paint  salesman from Minnesota named Ted killer  he gunned him down in front of a diner  while his wife her mother-in-law watched  why exactly he did this nobody is sure  to this day then when the gang did  commit their first robbery together the  Security National Bank in Sioux Falls  South Dakota Nelson let loose with his  tommy gun on a motorcycle patrolman  named hail Keith and as the officer  collapsed the ground he proudly shouted  I got one I got one with all the bodies  they kept dropping came increased heat  from the police not to mention that the  FBI got involved as well shootouts  between the two sides became more  frequent and more vile and ultimately  making it clear that it was only one way  this would end  foreign  was the first to go following a shootout  with the FBI at his hideout in Saint  Paul Minnesota in early April a couple  of weeks later the rest of the gang and  their wives and girlfriends were laying  low at the Little Bohemia Lodge in  Wisconsin someone tipped off the feds  about their presence which led to a  botch raid that turned into a bloodbath  the Lawman opened fire on a group of  innocent bystanders in a case of  mistaken identity killing a man named  Eugene boisner the gunshots tipped off  Dillinger and the Gang who returned fire  and managed to make it to their cars and  Escape leaving the women behind  meanwhile Nelson was the only one who  wasn't with the group when the shooting  started so he felt he had to make it on  his own he ran through the woods for a  while before stealing a vehicle and then  driving to a remote house where he took  everyone hostage unbeknownst to him  however the people inside called the  authorities as soon as they saw the  vehicle pull up in front of their home a  police car arrived on the scene with two  FBI agents in the local constable and  Nelson gleefully opened fire on them all  two of them were seriously wounded while  special agent W Carter bomb was hit in  the neck and died in minutes Nelson then  got into the car and drove away after  the shootout at Little Bohemia the gang  went their separate ways maybe they  planned on reuniting later who knows but  they never got the chance because they  started dropping like flies Hamilton  died in another gunfight just a few days  later then over the summer Tommy Carroll  Homer band meter and even Dillinger  himself all bit the big one following  shootouts with law enforcement all of a  sudden it was just Nelson his wife Helen  Gillis and John Paul Chase finally both  Face Nelson got to enjoy the notoriety  of being Public Enemy Number One for a  short while at least Nelson wisely  decided to keep a low profile and stay  on the move but that is easier said than  done when you're the most Wanted Man in  the country he had a close call in late  November in Lake Geneva Wisconsin when  he ran into some feds staking out a  former Hideout of his but he managed to  get away uncharacteristically without  firing a single shot but even so the  Noose was tightening around Nelson's  neck the FBI now at his car his number  plates and were hot on his tail they  caught up to him on November 27 1934 in  the town of Barrington Illinois and  staged one final shoot out that wouldn't  fill out a place in any action movie  with three cars one filled with  criminals two with FBI agents racing on  the highway side by side Nelson drove  while Chase took out one car with a few  well-placed shots but their own vehicle  took a bullet to the radiator that left  them partially disabled minutes later  their ride conked out so Nelson veered  off the highway into a park in  Barrington the second FBI car with agent  Samuel Cowley and Hermann Hollis pulled  up close to it but it was immediately  met with a spray of bullets from Nelson  to chase the Lawman a returned fire but  the crooks had the upper hands Hollis  was shot and killed during the battle  while Cowley was mortally injured Belton  and his accomplices got into the FBI car  and drove away seemingly Triumph them  once again but that was not the case  this time Chase and Helen Gillis might  have escaped unscathed but the same  could not be said for Nelson who had  sustained several gunshot wounds just a  few hours later Babyface Nelson was dead  his body was found the next day in a  cemetery in a nearby town both Helen  Gillis and John Paul Chase were arrested  soon after she served one year in prison  for harboring a known know while Chase  spent 32 years behind bars before being  released on parole in 1966. as for baby  pearls Nelson he liked to brag that he  would never be taken alive and he got  his wish a bloody but unsurprising end  Juan of the most ruthless criminals in  American history
 

